-- title:
--   One prime Hecke step in the kernel-ideal dictionary
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ are trivial. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and the condition that, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated and spanning the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal among such orders; let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the rationally represented additive maps $X_1\to X_1$ into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. Let $d$ be a unit of the algebra, $r\neq q'$ a prime, and $y,s$ units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $s$ in the box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ generated by $z\otimes\alpha$ ($z\in\Lambda_1$, $\alpha$ an integral adele), $r\cdot s^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, $s^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ and $r^{-1}s\notin\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. Then for every elliptic curve $W'$ over $\kappa$ and every nonzero rationally represented additive map $\chi':X_1(\kappa)\to W'(\kappa)$ such that $\theta_1$ carries $\{\rho\circ\chi':\rho$ rationally represented $W'\to X_1\}$ onto the elementwise conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap y\widehat{\Lambda_1})$, there is a finite additive subgroup $C$ of $W'(\kappa)$ with $\mathrm{card}\,C=r$ such that $\theta_1$ carries $\{\sigma\circ\chi':\sigma$ rationally represented $W'\to X_1$, $\sigma|_C=0\}$ onto the elementwise conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap ys\widehat{\Lambda_1})$.
--
--   This is one prime step of the Deuring kernel-ideal dictionary between right sublattices of the lattice attached to a finite idele $y$ and finite subgroups of a curve realising that lattice, stated in annihilator form and uniformly over all realisations $(W',\chi')$ with the fixed unit $d$. It is the per-step input for the chain argument that realises a normalised connecting idele of an Eichler order by iterating prime Hecke steps, used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_realisation_isAddCyclic_ker_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_realisation_isAddCyclic_ker_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele).
